    "answer": "## Household review\n\n- **Northwind jacket:** Started return **NW-R1001** for a **$105.34 refund** to the original payment method. Northwind says to print the label from its email and ship the jacket; a reminder is set for **October 27**, before the return window ends October 28.\n- **Harbor Bank fees:** Asked for a courtesy reversal of three $35 overdraft fees, totaling **$105**. Support reference: **HB-1002**. A follow-up is set for October 24.\n- **St Mary Hospital:** Asked billing for an itemized statement, financial-assistance instructions, and an account hold for the **$5,099.57** bill. Reference: **SM-1003**. I also asked you for household size and current annual income, which are needed to proceed with the assistance application.\n- **Keystone denial:** Asked St Mary to check the missing prior authorization and resubmit the **$1,266.81** claim if appropriate. Reference: **SM-1004**. The EOB\u2019s appeal window runs through **December 28**; a formal appeal would need your approval.\n- **ShopMart:** The promised **$46.36** refund posted September 6.\n- **QuickLoan settlement:** The July 31, 2026 claim deadline has passed, so I did not file.\n- **Recurring charges:** Saved the Spotify, Oakview rent, and Metro Power inventory for review. I found no indication these services are unwanted, so I took no cancellation action.\n\nThe review queue is clear. I couldn\u2019t record the Harbor Bank submission in the result tracker because it returned \u201cRecord not found,\u201d but the support site confirmed the message was sent.",
